{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6962-crossovers-outside-of-the-trinity-continuum","id":6962,"title":"Crossovers Outside of the Trinity Continuum?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-09T12:10:53-08:00","id":6962,"title":"Crossovers Outside of the Trinity Continuum?","content":"I've always liked trying to cross <b>MAGE</b> (generally the OWoD one) with Aberrant. After all, Zatanna is in the JLA. I've also tried Gods and monsters campaigns were Mages and Novas show up in 1910, society collapses, it's 1950 and the PCs are fighting to but the world back together. So, will it be possible to cross the new Trinty Continuum with the WoD?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-09T14:50:06-08:00","id":7043,"title":"","content":"Not likely. <b>Trinity Continuum</b> and <b>Scion</b> are getting redone to use OPP\u2019s new house system, which will reduce compatibility with the World of Darkness and Exalted lines. <br /> <br /> That said, note that I said \u201cand <b>Scion</b>\u201d. One of my hopes for <b>Scion</b> is that it will broaden its scope from <i>just</i> playing the children of the gods to acting as the basis for <i>any</i> game that heavily features real-world mythologies; from what I hear, they <i>do</i> intend to expand it so that sorcerers and holy men are more of a thing. <b>Trinity Continuum</b> focuses on superscience; <b>Scion</b> focuses on supernatural legends. I could <i>easily</i> see pairing the two of them up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T01:36:22-08:00","id":7236,"title":"","content":"Remain to be seen how compatible the two lines will be. However, if you wanted to play Avengers with Thor as a literal God...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T02:15:49-08:00","id":7247,"title":"","content":"\u2026or Wonder Woman as a scion\u2026 The earliest stories of Wonder Woman highlighted the source of her powers as her Amazon training permitting her to harness her \u201cmental energy\u201d to achieve incredible results. Conceptually, that\u2019s got \u201cArete\u201d written all over it. And the distinction between Hero and Demigod is not unlike the distinction between psiad and psion, or stalwart and Nova.<br /> <br /> <b>Trinity Continuum: Adventure!</b> could also benefit from crossovers; though in that case, it would be mostly Heroes, Guides, creatures, and Relics showing up. Heck, the cover of <b>Adventure!</b> shows ancient ruins in the background; Max Mercer might be exploring a Pesedjet Terra Incognito.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-10-2013, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-10T12:02:23-08:00","id":7546,"title":"","content":"I meshed all three into the WoD a while back in my FEAR Corporation fan book .. not a precise fit .. but it worked .. kinda .. :P<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T00:36:16-08:00","id":7917,"title":"","content":"I was toying with an Aeon/Firefly crossover idea for a while, but with my gaming group all dispersed we only seem to be able to get together a few times a year and doing something experimental like that does not seem practical so it probably will not go anywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T15:53:10-08:00","id":8429,"title":"","content":"I use Trinity as the basis for my exploration chronicles the basic universe modified by 20 years so it is not quite Trinity/Firefly crossover but it is fairly doable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T18:37:33-08:00","id":10119,"title":"","content":"How about using the Trinity rules to make an EVE RPG?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/722-walksforever","name":"Walksforever","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:17:59-08:00","id":12953,"title":"","content":"then will need an actual subsystem for spaceships... maybe as a fanon project I could see that happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T17:24:16-08:00","id":14392,"title":"","content":"I would relish Scion with Adventure! for a basis for our WW2 Scion game. It was a retarded amount of fun, regardless of the general disapproval of Internet folks of the Scion WW2 material","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1071-raleel","name":"Raleel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T18:18:24-08:00","id":14422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Walksforever</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6962-crossovers-outside-of-the-trinity-continuum?p=10119#post10119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about using the Trinity rules to make an EVE RPG?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think bolder.<br /> <br /> Think <b>Exile</b>! That's right - lodes, machina, Artifex, rules for playing a Sark'Saron...it's all there!<br /> <br /> (note: probably not going to happen)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T22:09:16-08:00","id":16463,"title":"","content":"Our ST was all gung-ho about the cWoD. When I bought Aberrant and fell in love with it, we decided to try to combine the two. The novas erupted and the governments began to use them to fight the monsters. The various supernatural critters saw the novas as a threat and, in an unprecedented show of solidarity, worked to try to end them.<br /> <br /> My character started out as a member of a strike force that would go out and fight them. Overall, it meshed well until we hit the upper core tier of Quantum 5 and started to throw down some serious powers. We then had to re-evaluate the power scales of the various systems and retired that game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T11:15:01-08:00","id":21778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/6962-crossovers-outside-of-the-trinity-continuum?p=16463#post16463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our ST was all gung-ho about the cWoD. When I bought Aberrant and fell in love with it, we decided to try to combine the two. The novas erupted and the governments began to use them to fight the monsters. The various supernatural critters saw the novas as a threat and, in an unprecedented show of solidarity, worked to try to end them.<br /> <br /> My character started out as a member of a strike force that would go out and fight them. Overall, it meshed well until we hit the upper core tier of Quantum 5 and started to throw down some serious powers. We then had to re-evaluate the power scales of the various systems and retired that game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant does have an unstable power level problem where some of the powers get too overpowered and others seem to plateau in effectiveness early and not go anywhere unfortunately; hopefully that will be solved in the new version. I translated the first set of characters from my group over into another popular superhero game system and some old favorites from that other system to Aberrant and repeated it later and the progressions in power over time do not track well across the systems.<br /> <br /> Between the mechanics difficulty, the vast difference in atmosphere and style between the systems, and the fact that they are the same general genre (at least on the surface anyway, Aberrant is actually more of a high-end transhuman space opera without the space part instead of a traditional superhero comic style) it was not worth the hassle of converting it for a functional campaign, it was better to just keep them separate (though the short appearance of the PCs from one system as guest NPCs in the other worked out ok).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","user":"BC001","date":". 12-02-2013, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/869-bc001","name":"BC001","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar869_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}